🔥 Sliding Window Technique 
==============================
❓ Sliding Window kya hota hai?

Sliding Window ek optimization technique hai jo array / string problems me use hoti hai jab:

Contiguous subarray / substring ka question ho

Brute force O(n²) ya O(n³) ja raha ho

Tum window ko slide karke kaam kar sakte ho

👉 Window = array ka ek continuous part

🧠 Real-Life Analogy

Socho tum train ke window se bahar dekh rahe ho 🚆

Pehle window ek jagah par hai

Fir train move karti hai → window ka view shift hota hai

Har baar new view milta hai bina pura train ghoomne ke

Bas wahi Sliding Window hai 😄

🪟 Types of Sliding Window (VERY IMPORTANT)
1️⃣ Fixed Size Sliding Window
📌 Example:

Size = k

Question: Maximum sum of subarray of size k


🧩 Example 1: Maximum Sum Subarray of Size K
Input
arr = [2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2]
k = 3

❌ Brute Force

* Har subarray ka sum nikaalo

* Time: O(n²) ❌

✅ Sliding Window Approach
==========================

int maxSum = 0, windowSum = 0;
int k = 3;

for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    windowSum += arr[i];

    if (i >= k - 1) {
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);
        windowSum -= arr[i - (k - 1)];
    }
}

🧠 Soch

* Pehle window banao

* Phir new element add

* old element remove

* Compare & slide

⏱ Time: O(n)
📦 Space: O(1)

2️⃣ Variable Size Sliding Window (Most Important ⭐⭐⭐)

Yaha window ka size expand / shrink hota rehta hai

📌 Used when:

* Condition based problems

* Longest / shortest subarray

* Sum / count / distinct
